<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Match Quadratic Graphs and Their Equations: Mini-Lesson Review</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02075</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Match Quadratic Graphs and Their Equations: Mini-Lesson Review</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0d1ad1cc-34df-4da2-a236-528a9d8823ab</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <note class="mini-lesson-question" id="note-00001">
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00001"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_OR_U8_Q3"/></para>
        </problem>
      </exercise>

    </note>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Match Quadratic Graphs and Their Equations</title>
      <para id="para-00004">The factored form helps find the zeros of a quadratic function.</para>
      <para id="para-00005">The factored form gives the zeros, and the <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>-intercepts are located where each factor equals 0.</para>
      <para id="para-00006">
        <emphasis>Example</emphasis>
      </para>
      <para id="para-00007">Examine the graph. What are the <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>-intercepts of the graph?</para>
      <para id="para-00008">
        <media alt="GRAPH OF A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UPWARD WITH A \(y\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 4 AND \(x\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 4 AND 1.">
          <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_09_02_08_01.jpg" width="300"/>
        </media>

      </para>
      <para id="para-00009">The graph crosses the <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>-axis at <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mo>−</m:mo>
            <m:mn>4</m:mn>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>. These are the <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>-intercepts.</para>
      <para id="para-00010">Look at each function to see which matches the graph. Look for the factors that have zeros as <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mo>−</m:mo>
            <m:mn>4</m:mn>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">a. <m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>This function has zeros at <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. The zero <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is not a zero on the graph.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">b. <m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
      <list id="list-00004">
        <item>This function has zeros at <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. The zero <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is not a zero on the graph.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00033">c. <m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
      <list id="list-00006">
        <item>This function has zeros at <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. The signs of the zeros of this function are the opposite of the signs of the zeros on the graph.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00034">d. <m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
      <list id="list-00008">
        <item>This function has zeros at <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. This function has zeros that match the zeros on the graph.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00011">The function <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>f</m:mi>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo>−</m:mo>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> matches the graph.</para>
      <note class="try" id="note-00002">
        <title>Try It: Match Quadratic Graphs and Their Equations</title>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00012">Examine the graph.</para>
            <para id="para-00013">
              <media alt="GRAPH OF A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UPWARD WITH A \(y\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 8 AND \(x\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 2 AND 4.">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_09_02_08_02.jpg" width="300"/>
              </media>

            </para>
            <para id="para-00014">Which function matches the graph?</para>
            <para id="para-00015"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00016"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00017"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00018"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00019">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00020">Here’s how to match the function to the graph.</para>
            <para id="para-00021">Look at each function to see which matches the graph. Look for the factors that have zeros at <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>.</para>
            <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00009">
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
            </list>
            <list id="list-00010">
              <item>This function has zeros at <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>. The zero <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> is not a zero on the graph.</item>
            </list>
            <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00011">
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
            </list>
            <list id="list-00012">
              <item>This function has zeros at <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>. The zero <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> is not a zero on the graph.</item>
            </list>
            <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00013">
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
            </list>
            <list id="list-00014">
              <item>This function has zeros at <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>. This function has zeros that match the zeros on the graph.</item>
            </list>
            <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00015">
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
            </list>
            <list id="list-00016">
              <item>This function has zeros at <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>. The zeros of the function have the opposite signs of the zeros on the graph.</item>
            </list>
            <para id="para-00022">The function <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math> matches the graph.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </note>
    </section>
    <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002">
      <title>Check Your Understanding</title>
      <exercise id="_85e6ea4a-1b2d-4462-93b2-3e7ee9cbb4b7" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00023">Examine the graph.</para>
          <para id="para-00024">
            <media alt="GRAPH OF A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UPWARD WITH A \(y\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 6 AND \(x\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 3 AND 2.">
              <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_09_02_08_03.jpg" width="300"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00025">Which function matches the graph?</para>
          <para id="para-00026">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <list list-type="enumerated" number-style="lower-alpha" id="list-00017">
          <item><para id="para-00027"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
